  <!-- ═══ ABOUT ═══ -->
  <section id="about" class="section about-section" data-chapter="about">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="chapter-tag fade-up">About</div>
      <div class="about-hero fade-up delay-1">
        <div><h2 class="about-title">I make messy spatial data <em>defensible.</em></h2><p class="about-lede">I work where municipal source maps, parcel geometry, and rigorous QA meet. At <strong>Nook Office Solutions</strong>, I turn fragmented zoning sources into clean, audit-ready datasets used across the USA, Canada, and other international regions.</p><div class="about-proof"><span class="proof-pill">2,000+ maps</span><span class="proof-pill">7,000+ cities sourced</span><span class="proof-pill">95–100% accuracy</span><span class="proof-pill">92% KPI</span></div></div>
        <figure class="about-portrait"><span class="portrait-geo ring-a" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="portrait-geo ring-b" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="portrait-geo diamond" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="portrait-geo nodes" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="portrait-geo cross" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="portrait-coord" aria-hidden="true">34.0151° N · 71.5249° E</span><img src="assets/thumbs/muddasir-portrait.jpg" alt="Professional portrait of Muddasir Ali" width="640" height="800" decoding="async"><i class="portrait-scan" aria-hidden="true"></i></figure>
      </div>
      <div class="about-principles fade-up delay-2">
        <article class="about-card"><h3>Source With Authority.</h3><p>I research municipal and county portals, REST services, and current map sources so every dataset begins with evidence that can be traced and trusted.</p></article>
        <article class="about-card"><h3>Build With Precision.</h3><p>Georeferencing, topology validation, and detailed checks for gaps, overlaps, and slivers keep parcel and zoning geometry accurate at scale.</p></article>
        <article class="about-card"><h3>Deliver With Context.</h3><p>Experience in disaster mapping, crop classification, NDVI analysis, and field collection helps me see beyond geometry to the decisions a map must support.</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="tools-row fade-up delay-3">
        <div class="tools-label">Working Stack</div>
        <div class="tools-tags">
          <span>ArcGIS Pro</span><span>ArcMap</span><span>QGIS</span><span>Google Earth Engine</span>
          <span>KoboCollect</span><span>Leaflet</span><span>Mapbox</span><span>Web Scraping</span>
          <span>AI-Assisted Automation</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ EXPERIENCE ═══ -->
  <section id="experience" class="section experience-section" data-chapter="experience">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="chapter-tag fade-up">Experience</div>
      <div class="experience-intro fade-up delay-1">
        <h2 class="section-title">Five Years.<br>One Spatial Journey.</h2>
        <div class="experience-copy"><p class="section-sub">From provincial disaster response to international zoning pipelines — each role sharpened the same core skill: accurate, defensible spatial data under real deadlines.</p><div class="exp-summary"><div class="exp-stat"><strong>6</strong><span>Assignments</span></div><div class="exp-stat"><strong>2K+</strong><span>Maps Digitized</span></div><div class="exp-stat"><strong>3×</strong><span>Recognition</span></div></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline fade-up delay-2">
        <div class="timeline-track"></div>
        <div class="timeline-fill" id="tl-fill"></div>

        <div class="tl-item active">
          <div class="tl-period">September 2025 – Present</div>
          <div class="tl-org">Nook Office Solutions</div>
          <div class="tl-role">GIS Analyst</div>
          <ul class="tl-desc">
            <li>Digitize, update, and QA parcel and zoning shapefiles across international regions including the USA and Canada, maintaining 95–100% spatial accuracy</li>
            <li>Georeference source maps and imagery, ensuring minimal RMS error before digitization begins</li>
            <li>Build and maintain QA workflows to detect topology errors, geometry slivers, gaps, and overlays across large parcel/zoning datasets</li>
            <li>Audit new team members' digitization output for accuracy and consistency as part of internal QA checks</li>
            <li>Source the most current zoning and parcel maps by researching and scraping authoritative municipal/county GIS portals (e.g., MapGeo) and REST feature services</li>
            <li>Identify and log updated data source links for 7,000+ cities, maintaining a 92% KPI over one year</li>
            <li>Digitized and QA'd 2,000+ maps to date; recognized as Employee of the Month three times for accuracy and output</li>
            <li>Collaborate cross-functionally with the broader data science and GIS team to align on zoning data standards and workflow improvements</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tl-tools"><span>Zoning &amp; Parcel Data</span><span>Topology QA</span><span>REST Services</span><span>Web Scraping</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-period">March 2025 – September 2025</div>
          <div class="tl-org">Excise, Taxation &amp; Narcotics Control Department, KP</div>
          <div class="tl-role">GIS Associate</div>
          <ul class="tl-desc">
            <li>Conducted field surveys using GPS and KoboCollect to capture property and land data</li>
            <li>Digitized surveyed property boundaries and linked spatial data to official government records</li>
            <li>Verified field-collected data against existing records to ensure accuracy and completeness</li>
            <li>Passed a competitive GIS technical assessment to be appointed into the role</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tl-tools"><span>GPS Survey</span><span>KoboCollect</span><span>ArcMap</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-period">July 2024 – March 2025 <span style="opacity:.6">(earlier stint: June – October 2022)</span></div>
          <div class="tl-org">Crop Reporting Services, Directorate of Agriculture, KP</div>
          <div class="tl-role">GIS Intern</div>
          <ul class="tl-desc">
            <li>Performed supervised classification of crop lands across 7 merged districts, D.I. Khan, Charsadda, and surrounding areas of KP</li>
            <li>Digitized major crop classification layers and prepared final classification outputs</li>
            <li>Compiled and mapped rainfall, minimum, and maximum temperature data from province-wide Excel datasets</li>
            <li>Conducted time-series NDVI analysis using Google Earth Engine, ArcGIS Pro, and ArcMap for crop monitoring and image stacking</li>
            <li>Led a land suitability analysis for tomato and pea cultivation using soil nitrogen content, pH level, and soil type as key parameters</li>
            <li>(2022 stint) Digitized crop land boundaries for Bajaur district in support of provincial crop reporting</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tl-tools"><span>Google Earth Engine</span><span>NDVI</span><span>ArcGIS Pro</span><span>Supervised Classification</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-period">May 2023 – June 2024</div>
          <div class="tl-org">Provincial Disaster Management Authority (PDMA), KP</div>
          <div class="tl-role">GIS Intern</div>
          <ul class="tl-desc">
            <li>Produced hazard maps for landslide and flood risk assessment across affected districts</li>
            <li>Digitized flood-affected areas, including damaged/destroyed bridges and damaged vs. undamaged housing structures</li>
            <li>Mapped warehouse locations distributing relief aid to flood-affected communities</li>
            <li>Supported emergency response planning through timely, accurate spatial data delivery during active disaster events</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tl-tools"><span>Hazard Mapping</span><span>ArcGIS Pro</span><span>Damage Assessment</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-period">Early 2023 (through March 2023)</div>
          <div class="tl-org">Survey of Pakistan (SOP), Peshawar</div>
          <div class="tl-role">GIS Intern</div>
          <ul class="tl-desc">
            <li>Supported ongoing GIS/survey operations under the department's technical team</li>
            <li>Gained exposure to national-level survey and mapping standards and protocols</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tl-tools"><span>Survey Standards</span><span>Field Mapping</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-period">4th Semester, 2022 (6 months)</div>
          <div class="tl-org">Board of Revenue, KP</div>
          <div class="tl-role">GIS Intern</div>
          <ul class="tl-desc">
            <li>Assisted in GIS lab operations related to land records and revenue mapping</li>
            <li>Gained early foundational exposure to government land administration GIS systems</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tl-tools"><span>Land Records</span><span>Revenue Mapping</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ PROJECTS ═══ -->
  <section id="projects" class="section projects-section" data-chapter="projects">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="chapter-tag fade-up">Featured Projects</div>
      <div class="projects-intro fade-up delay-1"><h2 class="section-title">Selected Work.<br>Measured Impact.</h2><p class="section-sub">Four case studies showing how I move from an open spatial question to a defensible method, clear evidence, and a decision-ready map.</p></div>

      <div class="projects fade-up delay-2">
        <div class="project" data-tilt>
          <div class="project-inner">
            <div class="project-top"><div class="proj-num">PROJECT 01</div><span class="project-type">Seismic Intelligence</span></div>
            <div class="project-visual results-visual"><a class="result-map primary" href="assets/awara-results/combined-precursors.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/thumbs/combined-precursors.jpg" alt="Combined multi-precursor analysis of the 2013 Awaran earthquake" width="884" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>Combined analysis</span></a><a class="result-map" href="assets/awara-results/study-area.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/thumbs/study-area.jpg" alt="Awaran district earthquake study area and fault line" width="1000" height="773" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>Study area</span></a><a class="result-map" href="assets/awara-results/lst-anomaly-map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/thumbs/lst-anomaly-map.jpg" alt="Pre-seismic land surface temperature anomaly map" width="773" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>LST anomaly</span></a></div>
            <div class="project-content"><div class="proj-title">Awaran Earthquake — Pre-Seismic Anomaly Detection</div><p class="proj-desc">Investigated whether satellite-observed geophysical behaviour contained meaningful signals before the Mw 7.7 Awaran earthquake. Five parameters were evaluated through statistical, machine-learning, and time-series models to separate potential precursors from ordinary variation.</p><div class="project-outcome"><strong>Outcome</strong><span>A comparative anomaly framework for identifying and communicating pre-seismic patterns across spatial maps and daily time series.</span></div><div class="proj-stack"><span>Remote Sensing</span><span>Anomaly Models</span><span>Google Earth Engine</span></div><a class="project-archive-link" href="awaran-results.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore all 23 research outputs <span>↗</span></a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="project" data-tilt>
          <div class="project-inner">
            <div class="project-top"><div class="proj-num">PROJECT 02</div><span class="project-type">Disaster Mapping</span></div>
            <div class="project-visual results-visual"><a class="result-map primary" href="assets/sindh-flood-results/flood-04.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/thumbs/flood-04.jpg" alt="Sindh 2022 flood extent mapped from satellite imagery" width="1000" height="693" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>Flood extent</span></a><a class="result-map" href="assets/sindh-flood-results/ndbi-04.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/thumbs/ndbi-04.jpg" alt="NDBI change during the Sindh flood period" width="1000" height="638" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>NDBI change</span></a><a class="result-map" href="assets/sindh-flood-results/ndvi-04.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/thumbs/ndvi-04.jpg" alt="NDVI change during the Sindh flood period" width="1000" height="624" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>NDVI change</span></a></div>
            <div class="project-content"><div class="proj-title">Sindh Floods 2022 — Impact &amp; Damage Assessment</div><p class="proj-desc">Combined Sentinel-2 imagery with NDVI, NDBI, and flood-extent mapping to trace environmental change from the pre-flood months through the 2022 event. The resulting sequence communicates shifting vegetation, built-up signatures, and inundation across Sindh.</p><div class="project-outcome"><strong>Outcome</strong><span>A multi-temporal evidence set supporting damage assessment, land-cover classification, and future flood-susceptibility modelling.</span></div><div class="proj-stack"><span>Sentinel-2</span><span>NDVI</span><span>NDBI</span><span>Flood Mapping</span></div><a class="project-archive-link" href="sindh-flood-results.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore all 22 flood outputs <span>↗</span></a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="project" data-tilt>
          <div class="project-inner">
            <div class="project-top"><div class="proj-num">PROJECT 03</div><span class="project-type">Site Intelligence</span></div>
            <div class="project-visual single-result"><a class="result-map" href="assets/landfill-results/landfill-site-selection.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/landfill-results/landfill-site-selection.png" alt="Landfill site suitability selection map" width="850" height="1100" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>Suitability result</span></a></div>
            <div class="project-content"><div class="proj-title">Peshawar Landfill Site Suitability Study</div><p class="proj-desc">Built a multi-criteria suitability model for responsible waste-disposal siting. Environmental and accessibility factors were weighted through AHP, normalized, and combined through weighted overlay.</p><div class="project-outcome"><strong>Outcome</strong><span>A ranked suitability surface highlighting the strongest candidate zones for further assessment.</span></div><div class="proj-stack"><span>AHP</span><span>Weighted Overlay</span><span>ArcGIS Pro</span></div><div class="results-note">Select the map to open the full-resolution suitability layout</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="project" data-tilt>
          <div class="project-inner">
            <div class="project-top"><div class="proj-num">PROJECT 04</div><span class="project-type">Species Distribution</span></div>
            <div class="project-visual results-visual"><a class="result-map primary" href="assets/termite-results/species-distribution.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/thumbs/species-distribution.jpg" alt="Distribution of four Reticulitermes species across China" width="1000" height="773" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>Four-species distribution</span></a><a class="result-map" href="assets/termite-results/r-flaviceps.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/termite-results/r-flaviceps.png" alt="Reticulitermes flaviceps colonies in Sichuan and Shaanxi" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>R. flaviceps</span></a><a class="result-map" href="assets/termite-results/r-aculabialis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/termite-results/r-aculabialis.png" alt="Asexual queen succession of Reticulitermes aculabialis" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span>R. aculabialis</span></a></div>
            <div class="project-content"><div class="proj-title">Reticulitermes Species Distribution in China</div><p class="proj-desc">Supported a Chinese postdoctoral researcher by converting documented records of <em>R. aculabialis</em>, <em>R. chinensis</em>, <em>R. flaviceps</em>, and <em>R. labralis</em> into a consistent spatial dataset and comparative distribution map.</p><div class="project-outcome"><strong>Outcome</strong><span>Publication-ready research cartography revealing geographic overlap and separation among four termite species.</span></div><div class="proj-stack"><span>Biogeography</span><span>Species Records</span><span>China</span><span>Research Cartography</span></div><div class="results-note">Select any result map to open the full-resolution layout</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ SKILLS ═══ -->
  <section id="skills" class="section skills-section" data-chapter="skills">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="chapter-tag fade-up">Full Capability Stack</div>
      <div class="skills-lead fade-up delay-1"><h2 class="section-title">Skills &amp;<br>Techniques.</h2><p class="section-sub">The geospatial methods I use to turn complex source data into accurate, repeatable, and defensible spatial evidence.</p></div>

      <div class="skills-wrap fade-up delay-2">
        <div class="skill-group" style="--skill:94%">
          <div class="skill-head"><span class="skill-icon"></span><div class="sg-label">GIS Platforms</div></div>
          <div class="sg-items">ArcGIS Pro · ArcMap · QGIS · Google Earth Engine (GEE) · KoboCollect/KoboToolbox · GPS Field Data Collection</div>
          <div class="skill-meta"><span>Core Stack</span><strong>Production Ready</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group" style="--skill:90%">
          <div class="skill-head"><span class="skill-icon"></span><div class="sg-label">Remote Sensing &amp; Spatial Analysis</div></div>
          <div class="sg-items">Supervised Classification · Land Suitability Analysis (AHP, Weighted Overlay) · NDVI/NDBI/NDWI Analysis · Time-Series Image Analysis · Image Stacking · Sentinel-2 Imagery Processing · Random Forest Classification · Hazard &amp; Risk Mapping</div>
          <div class="skill-meta"><span>Analysis</span><strong>Advanced</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group" style="--skill:98%">
          <div class="skill-head"><span class="skill-icon"></span><div class="sg-label">Data Digitization &amp; QA</div></div>
          <div class="sg-items">Digitization · Georeferencing (RMS Error Minimization) · Topology Validation · Sliver/Gap/Overlap Detection · Shapefile Updates &amp; Maintenance · Parcel &amp; Zoning Data QA · Data Accuracy Auditing</div>
          <div class="skill-meta"><span>Accuracy Focus</span><strong>95–100%</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group" style="--skill:86%">
          <div class="skill-head"><span class="skill-icon"></span><div class="sg-label">Data Sourcing &amp; Automation</div></div>
          <div class="sg-items">Web Scraping (Municipal/County GIS Portals, REST Feature Services) · Data Freshness Tracking · AI-Assisted Coding &amp; Automation · Workflow Automation for Data Pipelines</div>
          <div class="skill-meta"><span>Workflow</span><strong>Automated</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group" style="--skill:78%">
          <div class="skill-head"><span class="skill-icon"></span><div class="sg-label">Web Mapping &amp; Development</div></div>
          <div class="sg-items">Leaflet · Mapbox · HTML · CSS · JavaScript (Basics)</div>
          <div class="skill-meta"><span>Interactive Maps</span><strong>Applied</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group" style="--skill:84%">
          <div class="skill-head"><span class="skill-icon"></span><div class="sg-label">Data &amp; Reporting</div></div>
          <div class="sg-items">Excel Data Processing (Climate/Rainfall Datasets) · Spatial Data Linking to Official Records · KPI &amp; Accuracy Reporting</div>
          <div class="skill-meta"><span>Communication</span><strong>Decision Ready</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tools-divider fade-up delay-2"><div><div class="chapter-tag">Purpose-Built Systems</div><h3>Zoning Tools.</h3></div><p>Focused utilities I use to accelerate zoning QA, locate source data, recover map information, and reduce repetitive production work.</p></div>
      <div class="custom-tools-grid fade-up delay-3">
        <article class="custom-tool"><div class="tool-purpose">Zoning QA · Geometry Integrity</div><h4>Sliver Identification</h4><p>Finds narrow, unintended polygon fragments that can appear during digitization, editing, or boundary reconciliation.</p><div class="tool-detail">Pipeline: geometry thresholds · area/width checks · flagged output</div><span class="tool-status">Operational</span></article>
        <article class="custom-tool"><div class="tool-purpose">Zoning QA · Topology</div><h4>Overlap Detection</h4><p>Flags zoning polygons that occupy the same space so conflicting coverage can be reviewed and corrected efficiently.</p><div class="tool-detail">Pipeline: spatial intersection · duplicate coverage · QA report</div><span class="tool-status">Operational</span></article>
        <article class="custom-tool"><div class="tool-purpose">Zoning QA · Coverage</div><h4>Gap Detection</h4><p>Locates uncovered spaces between adjoining zoning polygons and helps verify continuous, complete geographic coverage.</p><div class="tool-detail">Pipeline: coverage envelope · difference analysis · gap polygons</div><span class="tool-status">Operational</span></article>
        <article class="custom-tool"><div class="tool-purpose">REST Services · Acquisition</div><h4>Data Downloader</h4><p>Downloads available layers from REST services and turns discovered service endpoints into reusable local source data.</p><div class="tool-detail">Handles: service discovery · layer selection · local export</div><span class="tool-status">Operational</span></article>
        <article class="custom-tool"><div class="tool-purpose">MapGeo · Source Recovery</div><h4>GeoMap Scraper</h4><p>Collects zoning map information from MapGeo sources when conventional downloads are unavailable or incomplete.</p><div class="tool-detail">Handles: map discovery · tile recovery · source logging</div><span class="tool-status">Operational</span></article>
        <article class="custom-tool"><div class="tool-purpose">Directories · Structured Extraction</div><h4>Data Extraction Engine</h4><p>Extracts useful zoning and source information from directory-style datasets and organizes it for downstream GIS workflows.</p><div class="tool-detail">Handles: directory traversal · metadata parsing · structured output</div><span class="tool-status">Operational</span></article>
        <article class="custom-tool in-progress"><div class="tool-purpose">Auto Digitizing · Active Development</div><h4>Zone Digitizer</h4><p>An assisted auto-digitizing system being developed to convert zoning source maps into editable spatial boundaries. Screenshots and validated results will be added when ready.</p><div class="tool-detail">Development focus: boundary extraction · cleanup · editable vectors</div><span class="tool-status building">In progress</span></article>
      </div>

      <div class="education-block fade-up delay-3">
        <div>
          <div class="edu-degree">BS Geomatics (GIS &amp; Remote Sensing)</div>
          <div class="edu-school">University of Peshawar · 2020–2024</div>
        </div>
        <div class="edu-elect">Electives: Land Information Systems<br>Advanced Photogrammetry</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ CONTACT ═══ -->
  <section id="contact" class="section contact-section" data-chapter="contact">
    <div class="container contact-inner">
      <div class="contact-stage fade-up">
        <div class="contact-copy">
          <div class="chapter-tag">Start A Conversation</div>
          <div class="availability-pill"><i></i>Available for remote opportunities</div>
          <h2 class="contact-heading">Have spatial data?<br>Let's make it <span class="accent">matter.</span></h2>
          <p class="contact-sub">Whether it is a zoning pipeline, a remote-sensing study, or a map that needs to hold up under scrutiny, I bring the careful spatial thinking that turns source data into confident decisions.</p>
